Reason:
The absence of a `break;` statement after successfully downloading cover art allows the code to continue executing subsequent logic, which can lead to errors or incorrect behavior when handling local cover art, as it may process further logic that is not intended to run if a cover has already been retrieved.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```java
if (coverBytes != null) {
    // Log cover download success
    break;
}
```
Reason:
Adding the `break;` statement ensures that once cover art is successfully downloaded (i.e., `coverBytes` is not null), the loop exits immediately, preventing any further processing that could lead to errors or unintended behavior.

